{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558638043,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf94c4bffeq3wW7wXHtAV6en","part":{"partID":"prt_1d407b678001hsyXwG3xZl4C1C","sessionID":"ses_e2bf94c4bffeq3wW7wXHtAV6en","messageID":"msg_1d40793510016ODMDVBKx8X1Eu","type":"tool","id":"call_da82b715c1424be1ae94bd78","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '1,80p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md"},"output":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Phase 14: review-remediation\"\ndescription: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that fix review pass one's work groups WG1 to WG13: the embed write safety, the attach-path guards, the renderer contract, the runner containment and the advisory fixes in checks, workflows, the baseline, readers, the subprocess, the bench and docs, each with a failing-then-passing test where one can exist.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"review remediation tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Phase 14: review-remediation\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n| `[C]` | Coordinator task: a gate, a full-suite run, an arena build or the close-out. No worker runs it |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nEvery command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. Each short name below is defined once.\n- `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `VX <file>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file>` in `ADV`. `VALL` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n- `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts` and `DA` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets`. `NT <file>` is `node --test <file>`. `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n- WG1: `EMB` is `$DS/agents-md-embed.cjs` and `EMBT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs`. `DAE` is `$DA/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`, `DAP` is `$DA/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt` and `DAC` is `$DS/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs`.\n- WG2: `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAG` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (new). `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `DER` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` and `DERIVE` is `node $DER --check | jq -r .status`, which must print `fresh`. `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` and `LR` is `$ADV/lib/README.md`. `SINGLE(m)` in a test is `{ action: 'route', selectionKind: 'single', targets: [{ workflowMode: m }] }`.\n- WG3: `RD` is `$ADV/lib/render.ts`. `GT` is `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`, `ENV` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` and `RCS` is `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`.\n- WG4: `RAD` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`. `R` is `$RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `ARB` is `$RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `S` is `$RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` and `BG` is `$ADV/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` (new). `MARK` is the file name `skilled-behaviour-arena`. `P7` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch`, read-only. `G2SUM` is `node $S --summary $P7/runs-g2.jsonl --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.g2.startRate)'`, which printed `{\"claude\":\"3 of 6\",\"codex\":\"0 of 6\",\"devin\":\"4 of 6\",\"dsh\":\"3 of 4\",\"opencode\":\"5 of 6\",\"pi\":\"4 of 6\"}` at planning.\n- WG5: `CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs`, `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` and `DSR` is `$DS/README.markdown`.\n- WG6: `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `CKT` its test `$DS/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `HWT` its test `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`.\n- WG7: `DSY` is `$DA/doctor-setup.yaml`, `DSM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md`, `DSP` is `$DA/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`, `DSC` is `$DA/doctor-symlink-check.yaml`, `DMR` is `$DA/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml` and `DSCT` is `$DS/tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs` (new).\n- WG8: `DIP` is `$DA/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `DIY` is `$DA/doctor-install.yaml` and `DICT` is `$DS/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`. `DEM` is `$DA/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` and `SARC` is `$DS/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`.\n- WG9: `CAP` is `$RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `BASE` is `$RAD/command-routing-baseline.json`, `CORPUS` is `$RAD/command-prompts.jsonl` and `SLT` is `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`. `HOLD` is the holdout id count in `spec.md` section 2, the `jq -n --slurpfile h ... --slurpfile b $BASE` line, which reads only `id` and `split` from `CORPUS`.\n- WG10: `RA` is `$RAD/README.md`.\n- WG11: `SR` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers` and `SRT` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers`. `VSR` is `node --test $SRT/*.test.mjs`, which must report `fail 0`. `SRD` is `node .skilled/hooks/shared/session-reader-declarations.mjs`, and `SRD --check` must print a line containing `current`. `SRR` is `$SR/README.md` and `PAR` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`.\n- WG12: `SUB` is `$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts` and `SUBT` is `$ADV/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` (new). `BENCH` is `$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` and `VB` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES=true npx vitest run bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` in `ADV`.\n- WG13: `SKA` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor`. `AR` is `$SKA/README.md`, `ARCH` is `$SKA/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CMM` is `$SKA/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md` and `ARM` is `$SKA/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`.\n- `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.typed, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune'`, which printed `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` and `{\"own\":8,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":23,\"total\":45}` at planning. `EVAL` is `node $RAD/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which printed `[160,50,21,5]`. `RV` is `bash $DS/route-validate.sh` and `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, both of which must exit 0.\n- `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder and `PL` is `$SP/planning`, which holds the six probes spec section 2 ran. Each probe's first comment line says how to run it.\n\nRules for every task:\n- Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test writes the test case first, runs it and sees it fail for the reason the task names, then makes the change and sees it pass. Its verify names both runs.\n- No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`. Count holdout rows by `id` and `split` only, and never open `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\n- No worker starts a model session (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin`, `dsh`), runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. A test builds its trees under a temporary folder and removes them.\n- No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T060 checks it.\n- Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, the parent `spec.md`, another phase, any `package.json`, `$ADV/lib/scorer/text.ts` or any routing input. Add no dependency.\n- A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n- Run Vitest with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD` unless a task says otherwise, because a dispatched worker inherits `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`.\n- When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n\nWorker lanes. A lane is one worker running its tasks in the order listed. Lanes in one wave own different files and run in parallel. Each task owns the files in its parentheses.\n- Wave 0, one worker: T001, T002. Read-only for the repository.\n- Gate: T003 [C].\n- Wave 1, the safety lane. WG1: T004, T005, T006, T007, T008. WG2: T009, T010, T011, T012, T013, T014. WG3: T015, T016, T017, T018. WG4: T019, T020, T021, T022, T023.\n- Wave 2, the advisory lane, after every wave 1 lane ends. WG5: T024, T025, T026, T027, T028. WG6: T029, T030, T031. WG7: T032, T033, T034, T035, T036, T037. WG8: T038, T039. WG9: T040, T041. WG11: T042, T043, T044, T045, T046, T047. WG12: T048, T049. WG13: T050, T051, T052.\n- Wave 3, after every wave 2 lane ends. WG10: T053, T054, T055.\n- Verification, one at a time: T056, T057, T058, T059, T060, T061, all [C].\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `SRD --check`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM`, `G2SUM`, `HOLD` and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse --short HEAD`, and write each command with its last output lines or its exit code into `before.txt`. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held. Verify: `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print the planning lines in Task Notation, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `DALL` and `VSR` report `fail 0`, `SRD --check` prints `current`, `DERIVE` prints `fresh`, `G2SUM` prints its planning line, `HOLD` prints `{\"holdout\":44,\"rows\":44,\"attachedRows\":0,\"typedRows\":0}` and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 13.\n- [x] T002 Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run the six probes in `PL`, then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV` and `VB`, and append each command and its output to `repro-before.txt`. Verify: `rg -c \"main threw: EACCES|target .cursor/rules/repo-local.md: replace|10 failed \\| 5 passed \\(15\\)|1 failed \\| 3 passed \\(4\\)|/create:agent \\(start\\)\" $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 5.\n- [x] T003 [C] Record the order against phase 015 (`$SP/before.txt`). Read phase 015's `tasks.md` and the worktree status, and append one line starting `order:` that names each spec section 3 file a phase 015 task also edits and which phase builds it first. No wave 1 task starts before this line exists. Verify: `rg -c \"^order:\" $SP/before.txt` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Phase 14: review-remediation\"\ndescription: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that fix review pass one's work groups WG1 to WG13: the embed write safety, the attach-path guards, the renderer contract, the runner containment and the advisory fixes in checks, workflows, the baseline, readers, the subprocess, the bench and docs, each with a failing-then-passing test where one can exist.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"review remediation tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Phase 14: review-remediation\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n| `[C]` | Coordinator task: a gate, a full-suite run, an arena build or the close-out. No worker runs it |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nEvery command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. Each short name below is defined once.\n- `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `VX <file>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file>` in `ADV`. `VALL` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n- `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts` and `DA` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets`. `NT <file>` is `node --test <file>`. `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n- WG1: `EMB` is `$DS/agents-md-embed.cjs` and `EMBT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs`. `DAE` is `$DA/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`, `DAP` is `$DA/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt` and `DAC` is `$DS/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs`.\n- WG2: `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAG` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (new). `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `DER` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` and `DERIVE` is `node $DER --check | jq -r .status`, which must print `fresh`. `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` and `LR` is `$ADV/lib/README.md`. `SINGLE(m)` in a test is `{ action: 'route', selectionKind: 'single', targets: [{ workflowMode: m }] }`.\n- WG3: `RD` is `$ADV/lib/render.ts`. `GT` is `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`, `ENV` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` and `RCS` is `$ADV/tests/render-child-session.vitest.ts`.\n- WG4: `RAD` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`. `R` is `$RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `ARB` is `$RAD/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `S` is `$RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` and `BG` is `$ADV/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` (new). `MARK` is the file name `skilled-behaviour-arena`. `P7` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch`, read-only. `G2SUM` is `node $S --summary $P7/runs-g2.jsonl --json | jq -cS 'map_values(.g2.startRate)'`, which printed `{\"claude\":\"3 of 6\",\"codex\":\"0 of 6\",\"devin\":\"4 of 6\",\"dsh\":\"3 of 4\",\"opencode\":\"5 of 6\",\"pi\":\"4 of 6\"}` at planning.\n- WG5: `CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs`, `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` and `DSR` is `$DS/README.markdown`.\n- WG6: `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `CKT` its test `$DS/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `HWT` its test `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`.\n- WG7: `DSY` is `$DA/doctor-setup.yaml`, `DSM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md`, `DSP` is `$DA/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`, `DSC` is `$DA/doctor-symlink-check.yaml`, `DMR` is `$DA/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml` and `DSCT` is `$DS/tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs` (new).\n- WG8: `DIP` is `$DA/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `DIY` is `$DA/doctor-install.yaml` and `DICT` is `$DS/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`. `DEM` is `$DA/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` and `SARC` is `$DS/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`.\n- WG9: `CAP` is `$RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `BASE` is `$RAD/command-routing-baseline.json`, `CORPUS` is `$RAD/command-prompts.jsonl` and `SLT` is `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`. `HOLD` is the holdout id count in `spec.md` section 2, the `jq -n --slurpfile h ... --slurpfile b $BASE` line, which reads only `id` and `split` from `CORPUS`.\n- WG10: `RA` is `$RAD/README.md`.\n- WG11: `SR` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers` and `SRT` is `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers`. `VSR` is `node --test $SRT/*.test.mjs`, which must report `fail 0`. `SRD` is `node .skilled/hooks/shared/session-reader-declarations.mjs`, and `SRD --check` must print a line containing `current`. `SRR` is `$SR/README.md` and `PAR` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts`.\n- WG12: `SUB` is `$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts` and `SUBT` is `$ADV/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` (new). `BENCH` is `$ADV/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` and `VB` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES=true npx vitest run bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` in `ADV`.\n- WG13: `SKA` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor`. `AR` is `$SKA/README.md`, `ARCH` is `$SKA/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CMM` is `$SKA/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md` and `ARM` is `$SKA/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`.\n- `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.typed, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune'`, which printed `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` and `{\"own\":8,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":23,\"total\":45}` at planning. `EVAL` is `node $RAD/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which printed `[160,50,21,5]`. `RV` is `bash $DS/route-validate.sh` and `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, both of which must exit 0.\n- `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder and `PL` is `$SP/planning`, which holds the six probes spec section 2 ran. Each probe's first comment line says how to run it.\n\nRules for every task:\n- Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test writes the test case first, runs it and sees it fail for the reason the task names, then makes the change and sees it pass. Its verify names both runs.\n- No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`. Count holdout rows by `id` and `split` only, and never open `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\n- No worker starts a model session (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin`, `dsh`), runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. A test builds its trees under a temporary folder and removes them.\n- No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T060 checks it.\n- Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, the parent `spec.md`, another phase, any `package.json`, `$ADV/lib/scorer/text.ts` or any routing input. Add no dependency.\n- A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n- Run Vitest with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD` unless a task says otherwise, because a dispatched worker inherits `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`.\n- When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n\nWorker lanes. A lane is one worker running its tasks in the order listed. Lanes in one wave own different files and run in parallel. Each task owns the files in its parentheses.\n- Wave 0, one worker: T001, T002. Read-only for the repository.\n- Gate: T003 [C].\n- Wave 1, the safety lane. WG1: T004, T005, T006, T007, T008. WG2: T009, T010, T011, T012, T013, T014. WG3: T015, T016, T017, T018. WG4: T019, T020, T021, T022, T023.\n- Wave 2, the advisory lane, after every wave 1 lane ends. WG5: T024, T025, T026, T027, T028. WG6: T029, T030, T031. WG7: T032, T033, T034, T035, T036, T037. WG8: T038, T039. WG9: T040, T041. WG11: T042, T043, T044, T045, T046, T047. WG12: T048, T049. WG13: T050, T051, T052.\n- Wave 3, after every wave 2 lane ends. WG10: T053, T054, T055.\n- Verification, one at a time: T056, T057, T058, T059, T060, T061, all [C].\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `SRD --check`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM`, `G2SUM`, `HOLD` and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse --short HEAD`, and write each command with its last output lines or its exit code into `before.txt`. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held. Verify: `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print the planning lines in Task Notation, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `DALL` and `VSR` report `fail 0`, `SRD --check` prints `current`, `DERIVE` prints `fresh`, `G2SUM` prints its planning line, `HOLD` prints `{\"holdout\":44,\"rows\":44,\"attachedRows\":0,\"typedRows\":0}` and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 13.\n- [x] T002 Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run the six probes in `PL`, then `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` in `ADV` and `VB`, and append each command and its output to `repro-before.txt`. Verify: `rg -c \"main threw: EACCES|target .cursor/rules/repo-local.md: replace|10 failed \\| 5 passed \\(15\\)|1 failed \\| 3 passed \\(4\\)|/create:agent \\(start\\)\" $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 5.\n- [x] T003 [C] Record the order against phase 015 (`$SP/before.txt`). Read phase 015's `tasks.md` and the worktree status, and append one line starting `order:` that names each spec section 3 file a phase 015 task also edits and which phase builds it first. No wave 1 task starts before this line exists. Verify: `rg -c \"^order:\" $SP/before.txt` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '1,80p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558637688,"end":1794558638043}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558638050,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf94c4bffeq3wW7wXHtAV6en","part":{"partID":"prt_1d407b4f8001rDRGtEIP84W266","sessionID":"ses_e2bf94c4bffeq3wW7wXHtAV6en","messageID":"msg_1d40793510016ODMDVBKx8X1Eu","type":"tool","id":"call_89f1f84795e24e9ba85de225","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"T048\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md"},"output":"62:- Wave 2, the advisory lane, after every wave 1 lane ends. WG5: T024, T025, T026, T027, T028. WG6: T029, T030, T031. WG7: T032, T033, T034, T035, T036, T037. WG8: T038, T039. WG9: T040, T041. WG11: T042, T043, T044, T045, T046, T047. WG12: T048, T049. WG13: T050, T051, T052.\n147:- [ ] T048 Cap the advisor child's stdout and stderr (`SUB`, `SUBT`). Test first: create `SUBT` with a case that writes a temporary script printing `JSON.stringify(['x'.repeat(2 * 1024 * 1024)])` and calls `runAdvisorSubprocess('prompt', { workspaceRoot: <temp>, pythonBin: process.execPath, scriptPath: <script>, timeoutMs: 10000 })`, expecting `errorCode` `JSON_PARSE_FAILED`, and a case whose script writes 2 MiB to stderr and exits 1, expecting `(result.stderr ?? '').length` at most `1024 * 1024`. Today the first reads another code because the whole array arrives. Then add `MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS = 1024 * 1024` and a `capOutput(current, chunk)` shaped like `capStdout` in `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, and use it in both `data` handlers of `runSpawnAttempt`, with a comment saying only the timeout bounded the child's output before, so a runaway child could hold the hook's memory until it was killed. Verify: before the change the first case fails, after it `VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"62:- Wave 2, the advisory lane, after every wave 1 lane ends. WG5: T024, T025, T026, T027, T028. WG6: T029, T030, T031. WG7: T032, T033, T034, T035, T036, T037. WG8: T038, T039. WG9: T040, T041. WG11: T042, T043, T044, T045, T046, T047. WG12: T048, T049. WG13: T050, T051, T052.\n147:- [ ] T048 Cap the advisor child's stdout and stderr (`SUB`, `SUBT`). Test first: create `SUBT` with a case that writes a temporary script printing `JSON.stringify(['x'.repeat(2 * 1024 * 1024)])` and calls `runAdvisorSubprocess('prompt', { workspaceRoot: <temp>, pythonBin: process.execPath, scriptPath: <script>, timeoutMs: 10000 })`, expecting `errorCode` `JSON_PARSE_FAILED`, and a case whose script writes 2 MiB to stderr and exits 1, expecting `(result.stderr ?? '').length` at most `1024 * 1024`. Today the first reads another code because the whole array arrives. Then add `MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS = 1024 * 1024` and a `capOutput(current, chunk)` shaped like `capStdout` in `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`, and use it in both `data` handlers of `runSpawnAttempt`, with a comment saying only the timeout bounded the child's output before, so a runaway child could hold the hook's memory until it was killed. Verify: before the change the first case fails, after it `VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"T048\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558637304,"end":1794558638050}}}}
