{"type":"text","timestamp":1794558831034,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf94c4bffeq3wW7wXHtAV6en","part":{"id":"prt_1d40a9adf002jhqThfjd1ja6Kb","sessionID":"ses_e2bf94c4bffeq3wW7wXHtAV6en","messageID":"msg_1d40a845c001636J7eam3ZskyQ","type":"text","text":"T048 is implemented and verified.\n\n**Files written**\n\n1. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts` — added `MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS = 1024 * 1024` and `capOutput(current, chunk)` (shaped like `capStdout` in the hook fallback), and both `data` handlers in `runSpawnAttempt` now append through it. Comment records why: only the timeout bounded the child's output before, so a runaway child could hold the hook's memory until it was killed.\n2. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` — new `SUBT` with the two cases the task names: a 2 MiB JSON array expecting `JSON_PARSE_FAILED`, and a 2 MiB stderr flood plus exit 1 expecting `(result.stderr ?? '').length <= 1024 * 1024`. Each script waits for stdin end before writing, so the parent's stdin write cannot race a closed pipe.\n\n**Before the change** (`VX tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts`)\n\n```\n ❯ tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts (2 tests | 1 failed) 61ms\n     × reports a parse failure when a large array is cut short 33ms\nAssertionError: expected 'INVALID_JSON_SHAPE' to be 'JSON_PARSE_FAILED'\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 1 passed (2)\n```\n\nThat is the reason the line predicts: the whole array arrived and parsed, so the shape check fired instead of the parse check.\n\n**After the change**\n\n```\n RUN  v4.1.12 .../runtime\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  2 passed (2)\n   Duration  183ms\n```\n\n`TC` (`npm run typecheck` in `ADV`) printed only the tsc invocation and exited `0`.\n\nScoped diff confirms only `lib/subprocess.ts` is modified and `tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` is new. The many other dirty paths in `git status` belong to other workers and were not touched. The checkbox in `tasks.md` was left unticked, as instructed.\n\nNothing was blocked. One caveat for the record: the stderr case also passes before the change, because `sanitizeStderr` already truncates the reported value to 240 characters. It still proves the cap does not break the failure path, but the first case is the one that fails without the change.","time":{"start":1794558827231,"end":1794558831034}}}
